# floor_derive.cam — the K3 acceptance fixture (DECISIONS.md → "K3, the
# material…", fork 4A): one derived S word on one real op, behind the opt-in.
#
# The stock declares what it is (material=6061) and the op replaces its
# spindle NUMBER with the word `derive` — so the shipped feeds table's
# 6061×Endmill row (surface_speed 150 m/min, conservative, sourced) resolves
# at validate to RPM = 1000·150/(π·10) = 4774.648, and the emitted M03 line
# carries S4774.648 while the global `spindle 3000` stays exactly what the
# ops WITHOUT the sentinel would get. Declared-outranks-derived by
# construction: one key, one source.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=120, l=80, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0, material=6061)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

# The Plane is the FINISHED face — stock top is z=0, so a 0.5mm skim names
# its face at z=-0.5 (the plate.cam stance).
feature TopFace Plane(z=-0.5)

run End(tool=T5, surface=TopFace, stepover=6.0, spindle=derive)
